  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=5-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $4$ | $1$ | $-4$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y={t}^{2}-3.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $4$ | $1$ | $-4$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/a39e8a0c4ed269e5cb73aaedf0655d85302f3a5c3c7e91d9f5e58ebf84a82423.png)",
